# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VIBLOC environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values you need.
# All `VITE_` prefixed vars are exposed to the client bundle, so
# they MUST be safe for public exposure (anon keys, public client
# IDs only — never service-role tokens or secrets).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase (auth + persistent storage) ─────────────────────────
#
# Required for the sign-in / sign-up / mypage flows. Without these
# the app still loads but every auth-gated UI shows "Supabase not
# configured" instead of a broken network call.
#
# How to get the values:
#   1. https://supabase.com/dashboard → New Project (region: Tokyo
#      or Seoul recommended for Asia traffic)
#   2. Settings → API
#      - "Project URL"        → VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#      - "anon / public key"  → VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#
# Both values are SAFE to ship in the frontend bundle. The anon
# key only carries row-level-security identity; real auth tokens
# come from the user's sign-in flow and live in localStorage.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Google OAuth (Sign in with Google) ───────────────────────────
#
# Required only for the "Sign in with Google" button. Without it,
# the email + password flow still works through Supabase.
#
# Setup:
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   2. Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID (type: Web application)
#   3. Authorized JavaScript origins:
#      - http://localhost:5173
#      - https://your-production-domain.example
#   4. Authorized redirect URIs:
#      - https://YOUR-SUPABASE-PROJECT.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ── Backend API base URL (optional) ──────────────────────────────
#
# Used by experimental server endpoints. Leave empty to skip.
# Example: https://api.vibloc.com
VITE_API_URL=

# ── Google Maps Embed (optional — Street View previews) ──────────
#
# Without this key, the building panel preview falls back to a
# Wikimedia Commons photo (where available) and an OpenStreetMap
# map tile (always), both of which are key-free and outdoor-safe
# but cannot show a real panorama.
#
# When set, VIBLOC uses Google's official Maps Embed API (Street
# View mode) to render the actual Street View panorama. Both
# endpoints (`embed/v1/streetview` + `streetview/metadata`) are
# FREE on Google Maps Platform.
#
# Setup:
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com/
#   2. Enable "Maps Embed API" + "Street View Static API"
#   3. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create API key
#   4. Restrict to HTTP referrers + Embed + Street View Static APIs
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_EMBED_KEY=
